# Allowlist for scripts/check-content-fallback.mjs (#3134).
#
# Entries here are reachable ONLY on a `--no-strict-content-bridge` build
# (i.e. `pnpm b4push`) — the native `strictContentBridge: true` gate in
# `zfb.config.ts` that covers plain `pnpm build` / CI has no allowlist at
# all. See the header of scripts/check-content-fallback.mjs for why both
# guards exist.
#
# One entry per line. An entry is matched as a plain substring against each
# offending page's dist-relative path, so a single entry covers every locale
# (`docs/foo/` also matches `ja/docs/foo/`). Blank lines and `#` comments are
# ignored.
#
# Only add a route here when the fallback is genuinely not shipped or not
# fixable from this repo, and say which in the `# reason:` line. A page that
# real users can load does NOT belong here — fix it instead.
#
# Stale entries are deliberately NOT reported: most exclusions here cover
# locally-generated routes that do not exist in a clean CI checkout, so an
# "unused entry" warning would fire on every CI run.

docs/claude-skills/
# reason: generated locally by the .claude watcher / `pnpm setup:doc-skill` and
# gitignored (.gitignore:35), so these routes exist only in a developer's tree
# and never in a CI build or the deployed site.
#
# Kept as defense-in-depth, not because the route is unprotected (#3259
# supersedes the earlier "most exposed due to size" framing — do not
# reintroduce it). Two structural defenses already guard generated skill
# pages: `escapeForMdx()` runs over every generated body
# (packages/zudo-doc/src/plugins/internal/claude-resources/generate.ts:580,
# subpages :610/:625/:640) and escapes braces and non-HTML tags to entities
# (escape-for-mdx.ts:53-86), and the output dir is wiped via a recursive
# `rmSync` and regenerated every build (`cleanDir` at generate.ts:497, helper
# at :65-68), so hand-placed raw MDX never survives. The entry stays because
# the upstream trigger (Takazudo/zudo-front-builder#2186, epic #3232) is
# shape-sensitive and size-driven (single concatenated dumps —
# l-lessons-zfb-migration-parity is ~150 KB) rather than tied to a specific
# character class, and `escapeForMdx()` only defends against one trigger
# class. A genuine fallback on this never-shipped local-only route must
# still not fail b4push. (They currently render fine; the pre-review text
# scan flagged them only because they *mention* the marker inside escaped
# <code> spans.)
